    "result_text": "Only `AcceptanceTest` is a concrete test (the others are the abstract base and a helper), and the full `mvnw test` run is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the soft-match (possible duplicate) rule on `POST /api/owners`. A new owner that isn't a hard duplicate but shares an existing owner's `lastName` and `postcode` while carrying a *different* `telephone` is now still created, and its `possibleDuplicate`/`possibleDuplicateOf` fields are set accordingly.\n\nChanges:\n\n- **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added two read-only fields to the `Owner` schema: `possibleDuplicate` (boolean) and `possibleDuplicateOf` (int32 id). The generated `OwnerDto` picks these up, and MapStruct auto-maps them by name.\n- **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added persisted `possible_duplicate` / `possible_duplicate_of` columns with getters/setters, so the flag survives to the `GET /api/owners/{id}` read-back.\n- **`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`** \u2014 added a `flagPossibleDuplicate(owner)` step after the hard-duplicate guard (`requireUniqueIdentity`) and before save. It defaults `possibleDuplicate` to `false`; when the owner has a postcode and some existing owner matches on last name (case-insensitive) + postcode with a different telephone, it sets `possibleDuplicate = true` and `possibleDuplicateOf` to that first-matching owner's id. Owners without a postcode never soft-match.\n- **`db/{hsqldb,h2,mysql,postgres}/schema.sql`** \u2014 added the two new columns (tests use the hsqldb schema with `ddl-auto=none`, so the column had to exist there).\n\nThe rule runs only after the hard-duplicate check passes, so a genuine 409 duplicate is still rejected and never reaches the soft-match path.",
